    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal strategy for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily on the top-tier matchup for **Corbin Carroll**, who anchors our lineup with a 79.07 efficiency score. Facing McGreevy and his 4.43 xERA, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from the prime leadoff spot and a projected platoon advantage that creates a high floor for Runs and SBs, our most critical category. **Vinnie Pasquantino** follows as our secondary engine at 66.63, leveraging a significant +14% dynamic platoon boost against Melton. While **Gabriel Moreno** also draws a favorable matchup against McGreevy to net a 61.30 score, the primary narrative today is the exploitation of vulnerable right-handed pitching, positioning these three as our most reliable engines for multi-category production.\n\nThe decision-making process for the remaining slots necessitated a tighter squeeze, particularly regarding **Zach McKinstry** (53.82) and **Austin Riley** (53.73). Despite the middle-of-the-road scores, **Zach McKinstry** earns the start largely due to the +19% boost from Dobnak\u2019s inflated 5.65 xERA; even with a suboptimal #8 spot in the order, the opportunity to capitalize on a struggling arm makes him a necessary play. Conversely, our bench remains largely barren today due to scheduled off-days for **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, and **Mickey Moniak**, leaving us without a competitive alternative to cycle in. We are monitoring **Travis Bazzana** (47.51) closely; his score is dragged down by a stiffer matchup against Bradley, but he stays in the lineup as our best remaining option for SB volume, ahead of unavailable assets like **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, or **Seiya Suzuki**.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the overall impact of order placement, as the -6% penalty for **Zach McKinstry** reflects the volatility of back-end lineup production. We have evaluated the potential for **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**, but none currently offer the projected floor required to displace our starters in a 5x5 format where every stolen base counts toward our weekly objectives. There are no immediate weather risks flagged for today\u2019s contests, so our focus remains strictly on the individual plate appearance efficiency of **Corbin Carroll** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** to carry the offensive load.",
